H6700.definition:
from H6697 (צוּר) and H410 (אֵל); rock of God;
Tsuriel, an Israelite
KJV: Zuriel.

H6701.definition:
from H6697 (צוּר) and H7706 (שַׁדַּי); rock of (the) Almighty;
Tsurishaddai, an Israelite
KJV: Zurishaddai.

H6702.definition:
a primitive root;
to blaze
KJV: burn.

H6703.definition:
from H6705 (צָחַח);
dazzling, i.e. sunny, bright, (figuratively) evident
KJV: clear, dry, plainly, white.

H6704.definition:
from an unused root meaning to glow;
parched
KJV: dried up.

H6705.definition:
a primitive root;
to glare, i.e. be dazzling white
KJV: be whiter.

H6706.definition:
from H6705 (צָחַח);
glaring, i.e. exposed to the bright sun
KJV: higher place, top.

H6707.definition:
feminine of H6706 (צְחִיחַ);
a parched region, i.e. the desert
KJV: dry land.

H6708.definition:
from H6706 (צְחִיחַ);
bare spot, i.e. in the glaring sun
KJV: higher place.

H6709.definition:
from an unused root meaning to putrefy;
stench
KJV: ill savour.

H6710.definition:
from H6705 (צָחַח);
a dry place, i.e. desert
KJV: drought.

H6711.definition:
a primitive root;
to laugh outright (in merriment or scorn); by implication, to sport
KJV: laugh, mock, play, make sport.

H6712.definition:
from H6711 (צָחַק);
laughter (in pleasure or derision)
KJV: laugh(-ed to scorn).

H6713.definition:
from an unused root meaning to dazzle;
sheen, i.e. whiteness
KJV: white.

H6714.definition:
from the same as H6713 (צַחַר); whiteness;
Tsochar, the name of a Hittite and of an Israelite
KJV: Zohar. Compare H3328 (יִצְחַר).

H6715.definition:
from the same as H6713 (צַחַר);
white
KJV: white.

H6716.definition:
from H6680 (צָוָה);
a ship (as a fixture)
KJV: ship.

H6717.definition:
from the same as H6678 (צוֹבָא); station;
Tsiba, an Israelite
KJV: Ziba.

H6718.definition:
from a form of H6679 (צוּד) and meaning the same;
the chase; also game (thus taken); (generally) lunch (especially for a journey)
KJV: [idiom] catcheth, food, [idiom] hunter, (that which he took in) hunting, venison, victuals.

H6719.definition:
from the same as H6718 (צַיִד);
a huntsman
KJV: hunter.

H6720.definition:
or צֵדָה; feminine of H6718 (צַיִד);
food
KJV: meat, provision, venison, victuals.

H6721.definition:
or צִידֹן; from H6679 (צוּד) in the sense of catching fish; fishery;
Tsidon, the name of a son of Canaan, and of a place in Palestine
KJV: Sidon, Zidon.

H6722.definition:
patrial from H6721 (צִידוֹן);
a Tsidonian or inhabitant of Tsidon
KJV: Sidonian, of Sidon, Zidonian.

H6723.definition:
from an unused root meaning to parch;
aridity; concretely, a desert
KJV: barren, drought, dry (land, place), solitary place, wilderness.

H6724.definition:
from the same as H6723 (צִיָּה);
a desert
KJV: dry place.

H6725.definition:
from the same as H6723 (צִיָּה) in the sense of conspicuousness (compare H5329 (נָצַח));
a monumental or guiding pillar
KJV: sign, title, waymark.

H6726.definition:
the same (regularly) as H6725 (צִיּוּן)lemma צִיוּן missing dagesh, corrected to צִיּוּן;
Tsijon (as a permanent capital), a mountain of Jerusalem
KJV: Zion.

H6727.definition:
or צִחָא; as if feminine of H6704 (צִחֶה); drought;
Tsicha, the name of two Nethinim
KJV: Ziha.

H6728.definition:
from the same as H6723 (צִיָּה);
a desert-dweller, i.e. nomad or wild beast
KJV: wild beast of the desert, that dwell in (inhabiting) the wilderness.

H6729.definition:
from an unused root meaning to confine;
the pillory
KJV: stocks.

H6730.definition:
from H6819 (צָעַר); small;
Tsior, a place in Palestine
KJV: Zior.

H6731.definition:
or צִץ; from H6692 (צוּץ);
properly, glistening, i.e. a burnished plate; also a flower (as bright-colored); a wing (as gleaming in the air)
KJV: blossom, flower, plate, wing.

H6732.definition:
the same as H6731 (צִיץ); bloom;
Tsits, a place in Palestine
KJV: Ziz.

H6733.definition:
feminine of H6731 (צִיץ);
a flower
KJV: flower.

H6734.definition:
feminine of H6731 (צִיץ);
a floral or wing-like projection, i.e. a forelock of hair, a tassel
KJV: fringe, lock.

H6735.definition:
from H6696 (צוּר);
a hinge (as pressed in turning); also a throe (as a phys. or mental pressure); also a herald or erranddoer (as constrained by the principal)
KJV: ambassador, hinge, messenger, pain, pang, sorrow. Compare H6736 (צִיר).

H6736.definition:
the same as H6735 (צִיר);
a form (of beauty; as if pressed out, i.e. carved); hence, an (idolatrous) image
KJV: beauty, idol.

H6737.definition:
a denominative from H6735 (צִיר) in the sense of ambassador;
to make an errand, i.e. betake oneself
KJV: make as if...had been ambassador.

H6738.definition:
from H6751 (צָלַל);
shade, whether literal or figurative
KJV: defence, shade(-ow).

H6739.definition:
(Aramaic) probably corresponding to H6760 (צָלַע) in the sense of bowing;
pray
KJV: pray.

H6740.definition:
a primitive root;
to roast
KJV: roast.

H6741.definition:
feminine of H6738 (צֵל);
Tsillah, an antediluvian woman
KJV: Zillah.

H6742.definition:
from H6749 (צָלַל) in the sense of rolling;
a (round or flattened) cake
KJV: cake.

H6743.definition:
or צָלֵחַ; a primitive root;
to push forward, in various senses (literal or figurative, transitive or intransitive)
KJV: break out, come (mightily), go over, be good, be meet, be profitable, (cause to, effect, make to, send) prosper(-ity, -ous, -ously).

H6744.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6743 (צָלַח);
to advance (transitive or intransitive)
KJV: promote, prosper.

H6745.definition:
from H6743 (צָלַח);
something protracted or flattened out, i.e. a platter
KJV: pan.

H6746.definition:
from H6743 (צָלַח);
something prolonged or tall, i.e. a vial or salt-cellar
KJV: cruse.

H6747.definition:
from H6743 (צָלַח);
something advanced or deep, i.e. a bowl; figuratively, the bosom
KJV: bosom, dish.

H6748.definition:
passive participle of H6740 (צָלָה);
roasted
KJV: roast.

H6749.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to tumble down, i.e. settle by awaving motion
KJV: sink. Compare H6750 (צָלַל), H6751 (צָלַל).

H6750.definition:
a primitive root (identical with through the idea of vibration);
to tinkle, i.e. rattle together (as the ears in reddening with shame, or the teeth in chattering with fear)
KJV: quiver, tingle.

H6751.definition:
a primitive root (identical with through the idea of hovering over (compare H6754 (צֶלֶם)));
to shade, as twilight or an opaque object
KJV: begin to be dark, shadowing.

H6753.definition:
from H6752 (צֵלֶל) and the active participle of H6437 (פָּנָה); shade-facing;
Tselelponi, an Israelitess
KJV: Hazelelponi (including the article).

H6754.definition:
from an unused root meaning to shade;
a phantom, i.e. (figuratively) illusion, resemblance; hence, a representative figure, especially an idol
KJV: image, vain shew.

H6755.definition:
(Aramaic) or צְלֶם; (Aramaic), corresponding to H6754 (צֶלֶם);
an idolatrous figure
KJV: form, image.

H6756.definition:
from H6754 (צֶלֶם); shady;
Tsalmon, the name of a place in Palestine and of an Israelite
KJV: Zalmon.

H6757.definition:
from H6738 (צֵל) and H4194 (מָוֶת);
shade of death, i.e. the grave (figuratively, calamity)
KJV: shadow of death.

H6758.definition:
feminine of H6757 (צַלְמָוֶת); shadiness;
Tsalmonah, a place in the Desert
KJV: Zalmonah.

H6759.definition:
from H6738 (צֵל) and H4513 (מָנַע); shade has been denied;
Tsalmunna, a Midianite
KJV: Zalmunna.

H6761.definition:
from H6760 (צָלַע);
a limping or full (figuratively)
KJV: adversity, halt(-ing).

H6762.definition:
the same as H6761 (צֶלַע);
Tsela, a place in Palestine
KJV: Zelah.

H6763.definition:
or (feminine) צַלְעָה; from H6760 (צָלַע);
a rib (as curved), literally (of the body) or figuratively (of a door, i.e. leaf); hence, a side, literally (of a person) or figuratively (of an object or the sky, i.e. quarter); architecturally, a (especially floor or ceiling) timber or plank (single or collective, i.e. a flooring)
KJV: beam, board, chamber, corner, leaf, plank, rib, side (chamber).

H6764.definition:
from an unused root of unknown meaning;
Tsalaph, an Israelite
KJV: Zalaph.

H6765.definition:
from the same as H6764 (צָלָף) and H259 (אֶחָד);
Tselophchad, an Israelite
KJV: Zelophehad.

H6766.definition:
from H6738 (צֵל) and H6703 (צַח); clear shade;
Tseltsach, a place in Palestine
KJV: Zelzah.

H6767.definition:
from H6750 (צָלַל) reduplicated;
a clatter, i.e. (abstractly) whirring (of wings); (concretely) a cricket; also a harpoon (as rattling), a cymbal (as clanging)
KJV: cymbal, locust, shadowing, spear.

H6768.definition:
from an unused root meaning to split; fissure;
Tselek, an Israelite
KJV: Zelek.

H6769.definition:
from the feminine of H6738 (צֵל); shady;
Tsillethai, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Zilthai.

H6770.definition:
a primitive root;
to thirst (literally or figuratively)
KJV: (be a-, suffer) thirst(-y).

H6771.definition:
from H6770 (צָמֵא);
thirsty (literally or figuratively)
KJV: (that) thirst(-eth, -y).

H6772.definition:
from H6770 (צָמֵא);
thirst (literally or figuratively)
KJV: thirst(-y).

H6773.definition:
feminine of H6772 (צָמָא);
thirst (figuratively, of libidinousnes)
KJV: thirst.

H6774.definition:
from H6771 (צָמֵא);
a thirsty place, i.e. desert
KJV: drought, dry ground, thirsty land.

H6775.definition:
a primitive root;
to link, i.e. gird; figuratively, to serve, (mentally) contrive
KJV: fasten, frame, join (self).

H6776.definition:
a yoke or team (i.e. pair);
hence, an acre (i.e. day's task for a yoke of cattle to plough)
KJV: acre, couple, [idiom] together, two (donkeys), yoke (of oxen).

H6777.definition:
from an unused root meaning to fasten on;
a veil
KJV: locks.

H6778.definition:
from H6784 (צָמַק);
a cake of dried grapes
KJV: bunch (cluster) of raisins.

H6779.definition:
a primitive root;
to sprout (transitive or intransitive, literal or figurative)
KJV: bear, bring forth, (cause to, make to) bud (forth), (cause to, make to) grow (again, up), (cause to) spring (forth, up).

H6780.definition:
from H6779 (צָמַח);
a sprout (usually concrete), literal or figurative
KJV: branch, bud, that which (where) grew (upon), spring(-ing).

H6781.definition:
or צָמִד; from H6775 (צָמַד);
a bracelet or arm-clasp; generally, a lid
KJV: bracelet, covering.

H6782.definition:
from the same as H6777 (צַמָּה);
a noose (as fastening); figuratively, destruction
KJV: robber.

H6783.definition:
or צְמִתֻת; from H6789 (צָמַת);
excision, i.e. destruction; used only (adverbially) with prepositional prefix to extinction, i.e. perpetually
KJV: ever.

H6784.definition:
a primitive root;
to dry up
KJV: dry.

H6785.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning to be shaggy;
wool
KJV: wool(-len).

H6786.definition:
patrial from an unused name of a place in Palestine;
a Tsemarite or branch of the Canaanites
KJV: Zemarite.

H6787.definition:
dual of H6785 (צֶמֶר); double fleece;
Tsemarajim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Zemaraim.

H6788.definition:
from the same as H6785 (צֶמֶר);
fleeciness, i.e. foliage
KJV: highest branch, top.

H6789.definition:
a primitive root;
to extirpate (literally or figuratively)
KJV: consume, cut off, destroy, vanish.

H6790.definition:
from an unused root meaning to prick; a crag;
Tsin, a part of the Desert
KJV: Zin.

H6791.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be prickly;
a thorn; hence, a cactus-hedge
KJV: thorn.

H6792.definition:
or צֹנֶה; for H6629 (צֹאן);
a flock
KJV: sheep.

H6793.definition:
feminine of H6791 (צֵן);
a hook (as pointed); also a (large) shield (as if guarding by prickliness); also cold (as piercing)
KJV: buckler, cold, hook, shield, target.

H6794.definition:
from an unused root perhaps meaning to be hollow;
a culvert
KJV: gutter, water-spout.

H6795.definition:
a primitive root;
to alight; (transitive) to cause to descend, i.e. drive down
KJV: fasten, light (from off).

H6796.definition:
or צָנִן; from the same as H6791 (צֵן);
a thorn
KJV: thorn.

H6797.definition:
or צָנוֹף; or (feminine) צָנִיפָה; from H6801 (צָנַף);
a head-dress (i.e. piece of cloth wrapped around)
KJV: diadem, hood, mitre.

H6798.definition:
a primitive root;
to blast or shrink
KJV: withered.

H6799.definition:
probably for H6630 (צַאֲנָן);
Tsenan, a place near Palestine
KJV: Zenan.
